tools.description:
Full-text search across all askWheat resources (genes, germplasm, genotyping datasets, files).

Filters (exact values): database e.g. 'Ensembl Plants', 'Watkins Wheat Pangenome', 'CropSNPdb', 'GBIF genebank accessions';
entry_type e.g. 'Gene annotation', 'Germplasm', 'Genotyping Experiment', 'File';

Position(s) of a genetic marker (90K/80K/9K iSelect, 35K Axiom, KASP, DArT, SSR e.g. 'BS00000713', 'wmc617', 'Xgwm149';
40K array IDs such as 'IWB61980' or 'AVRIG14047' come from CropSNPdb)
on IWGSC RefSeq v2.1 (IWGSC GMAP alignments), with genes within +/- flank bp of each hit.

Marker-trait associations from the OzWheat GWAS (285 Australian and international wheat cultivars and lines;
glasshouse 2016 and field trials at Canberra 2018-19, Wagga 2018, Narrabri 2019). Traits: days to anthesis,
days to heading, degree-days to heading ('flowering'/'heading') and plant height. F

BLAST a DNA or protein sequence (raw or FASTA; up to 20 kb DNA or 5,000 aa) against this site's databases:
Chinese Spring RefSeq v1.0 genome, RefSeq v1.1 CDS and proteins. The program is chosen from the query and database types (blastn, or blastn-short under 50 nt;
